      "math_academy_id": "q-14412",
      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Given that $\\frac{mn-4n}{2m}=a$ and $\\frac{2}{m-4}=b$, what is $a\\cdot b?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor all of the expressions and cancel any terms that appear in both a numerator and a denominator. Then, we multiply the numerators and the denominators as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =\\frac{mn-4n}{2m}\\cdot \\frac{2}{m-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{n(m-4)}{2\\cdot m}\\cdot \\frac{2}{m-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{n\\cancel{(m-4)}}{\\cancel{2}\\cdot m}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{2}}{\\cancel{m-4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{n}{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
